<div class="doc">
  <section class="doc-hero">
    <div class="doc-hero__crumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span class="doc-sep">/</span><span class="doc-cur">Maintenance &amp; Cleaning</span></div>
    <div class="doc-hero__head">
      <div class="doc-eyebrow"><span class="doc-eyebrow__ln"></span>Care Guide<span class="doc-eyebrow__ln"></span></div>
      <h1 class="doc-hero__title">Mosaic <span class="doc-i">Maintenance &amp; Cleaning</span></h1>
      <p class="doc-hero__sub">How to clean and care for handcrafted marble and glass mosaic tile — simple routine cleaning, marble sealing, pool and outdoor care, and what to avoid — so your mosaic stays brilliant for a lifetime.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="doc-wrap">
    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">The Essentials</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Everyday Care</h2>
      <p class="doc-sec__p">iMosaicArt mosaics are built to last and genuinely <strong>low-maintenance</strong>. For day-to-day care, simply wipe the surface with a soft cloth and warm water, or a mild <strong>pH-neutral</strong> cleaner. The golden rule across both materials: gentle, pH-neutral products and soft cloths only — never acidic cleaners or abrasive pads.</p>
      <ol class="doc-steps">
        <li>Remove loose dust and debris with a soft, dry cloth or soft brush.</li>
        <li>Wash with warm water and a mild, pH-neutral soap or stone cleaner, using a soft cloth or sponge.</li>
        <li>Rinse with clean water to remove any soap residue.</li>
        <li>Dry with a soft cloth — and buff glass gently for extra shine.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-cards">
        <div class="doc-card">
          <h3 class="doc-card__t" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;">Cleaning Marble Mosaics</h3>
          <p class="doc-sec__p" style="margin:0;">Marble is <strong>natural stone and acid-sensitive</strong>. Clean with a pH-neutral stone cleaner or mild soap and warm water on a soft cloth, then dry. <strong>Never use vinegar, lemon, bleach, or acidic cleaners</strong> — they etch and dull marble. Blot spills promptly instead of wiping, and seal periodically (see below).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <h3 class="doc-card__t" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;">Cleaning Glass Mosaics</h3>
          <p class="doc-sec__p" style="margin:0;">Glass is <strong>non-porous and waterproof</strong>, so it's the easiest to care for. Clean with warm water and a mild pH-neutral detergent on a soft cloth or sponge, rinse, and buff dry for a brilliant shine. For stubborn grime, use a soft brush or an ammonia-free glass cleaner. Avoid abrasive scourers or scouring powders, which can scratch the glass.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">Protecting Natural Stone</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Sealing Marble</h2>
      <p class="doc-sec__p">Because marble is porous, we recommend sealing marble mosaics periodically with a quality <strong>penetrating stone sealer</strong> — typically every one to two years, or more often in high-use and wet areas such as showers, pool surrounds, and kitchen backsplashes. Sealing protects against staining and keeps the stone looking its best. Glass mosaics do not require sealing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">Pools, Baths &amp; Exteriors</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Outdoor &amp; Pool Care</h2>
      <p class="doc-sec__p">Our mosaics are <strong>fully waterproof and weatherproof</strong>, so outdoor, bathroom, and pool pieces need only simple care. Rinse off dust and salt periodically, lift away any algae or buildup with a soft brush, and maintain normal pool water chemistry. The materials withstand sun, frost, heat, and humidity, so no special winter treatment is needed beyond clearing debris.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">Quick Reference</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Do's &amp; Don'ts</h2>
      <div class="doc-cards">
        <div class="doc-card doc-card--do">
          <div class="doc-card__t">Do</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Use pH-neutral cleaners and mild soap</li>
            <li>Clean with soft cloths or sponges</li>
            <li>Blot spills promptly, especially on marble</li>
            <li>Seal marble periodically in wet areas</li>
            <li>Test any new cleaner on a small spot first</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card doc-card--dont">
          <div class="doc-card__t">Don't</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Use vinegar, lemon, or acidic cleaners on marble</li>
            <li>Use bleach or ammonia on natural stone</li>
            <li>Scrub with abrasive pads or steel wool</li>
            <li>Use harsh scouring powders</li>
            <li>Let spills sit on marble surfaces</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">Common Questions</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Care FAQ</h2>
      <div class="doc-faq">
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">How do I clean a glass mosaic?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Wipe with warm water and a mild, pH-neutral soap using a soft cloth or sponge, then rinse and buff dry for shine. Glass is non-porous, so it cleans easily — just avoid abrasive pads that can scratch it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">How do I clean a marble mosaic?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Use a pH-neutral stone cleaner or mild soap and warm water on a soft cloth, then dry. Marble is acid-sensitive, so never use vinegar, lemon, bleach, or acidic cleaners, which etch and dull the stone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Can I use vinegar or lemon to clean marble?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">No — acidic cleaners like vinegar and lemon etch and dull natural marble. Use only pH-neutral products on marble. Glass tolerates mild cleaners, but pH-neutral soap and water is all it needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Do marble mosaics need sealing?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Yes. Marble is porous, so seal it periodically with a penetrating stone sealer — especially in showers, pools, and kitchens — to protect against staining. Glass mosaics do not need sealing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">How do I care for a pool or outdoor mosaic?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">They're waterproof and weatherproof, so care is simple: rinse off dust and salt, remove algae with a soft brush, and keep normal pool chemistry. No special winter care is needed beyond clearing debris.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">How do I remove a stain from marble?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Blot spills promptly rather than wiping. For light marks, use a pH-neutral stone cleaner; for set-in stains, use a stone poultice per its instructions. Avoid acidic or abrasive products.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
